[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Node Infrastructure and RPC Management in Blockchain"},{"order":2,"type":"subheading","text":"Introduction"},{"order":3,"type":"paragraph","text":"Reliable node infrastructure and Remote Procedure Call (RPC) management form the backbone of any decentralized application. Without a scalable, highly available node architecture, applications face latency bottlenecks, rate limiting, and catastrophic single points of failure during network congestion."},{"order":4,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Architecture Components"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Archive Nodes: Store the complete history of the blockchain state from genesis, essential for historical queries and debugging."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Full Nodes: Maintain a pruned or full state of recent blocks, balancing storage requirements with query capabilities."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Load Balancers: Distribute incoming RPC traffic across multiple node instances to prevent overload and ensure high availability."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Configuring an Nginx Load Balancer for RPC Endpoints"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Using a reverse proxy like Nginx allows you to manage traffic routing, SSL termination, and basic rate limiting for your Ethereum or EVM-compatible nodes."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"upstream rpc_backends {
    server 10.0.0.10:8545 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
    server 10.0.0.11:8545 max_fails=3 fail_timeout=10s;
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name rpc.yourdomain.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://rpc_backends;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Connection "";
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for RPC Management"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implement Fallback Providers: Combine self-hosted nodes with decentralized RPC providers like Infura, Alchemy, or Pocket Network to guarantee uptime."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Rate Limiting and Authentication: Secure your public-facing endpoints using API keys or JWT tokens to prevent Denial of Service (DoS) attacks and resource exhaustion."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Health Checking: Continuously monitor node synchronization status using eth_syncing or equivalent methods to route traffic away from lagging nodes."},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mastering node infrastructure ensures your Web3 applications remain performant and resilient. By decoupling your application layer from raw node operations through intelligent load balancing and fallback strategies, you safeguard your protocol against unexpected infrastructural failures."}]
